            "is_private": false,
            "creation_time": "2021-05-06T02:07:11Z",
            "text": "Created attachment 2837\npatch to ensure already sorted increasing ints receive ALTREP wrapper\n\nContext: sort.int\n\nCurrently the sorted_fpass internal checks integer vectors for being already sorted(increasing) in order to return quickly from sort.int in the as.factor case (among others).\n\nBut code that receives the fast-pass result wasn't updatead to understand that it could receive true from a non-altrep so the vectors are not being returned a known-sorted ALTREP form (a contract of sort for ints and numerics since we introduced that change).\n\nThis patch changes the fastpass to have 3 possible outcomes: 0 (no shortcut do sort), 1 (ALTREP that is already known-sorted) and 2 (is already sorted but needs a wrapper).\n\nPassed make check-devel for me and exhibits fixed behavior",
            "bug_id": 18096,
            "count": 0
          }
        ]
      }
